    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nTelephone numbers are now stored, returned, and compared in **E.164** form. I kept structural impact low by putting the new behaviour in small, cohesive units rather than growing existing methods or classes.\n\n**New domain units** (each with near-zero surrounding complexity):\n- `model/E164.java` \u2014 a pure helper. `toE164(raw)` keeps a leading `+` and country code when present; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; strips spaces, dashes and brackets; requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, throwing otherwise. So `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678` and `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`.\n- `model/InvalidTelephoneException.java` \u2014 a domain exception for unformattable input.\n\n**Small edits to existing code:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 `setTelephone` now delegates one line to `E164.toE164(...)`, so **both** create (via MapStruct's setter call) and update normalize through a single point. Dropped the obsolete 10-digit `@Digits`/`@Pattern` constraints (and their imports); the setter is now the source of truth. (Entities load via field access, so existing DB rows aren't re-validated.)\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 removed the old `qualifiedByName = \"normalizeTelephone\"` mapping and its digits-only method; `telephone` now maps by name straight through the normalizing setter.\n- `rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` \u2014 added one focused handler mapping `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400** (needed because the class's catch-all `Exception` handler would otherwise turn it into a 500).\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 relaxed the input pattern from exactly-10-digits to a permissive `^[-+()\\d ]+$`, so any E.164-formable input reaches the domain rule, which owns final validation.\n\n**Duplicate detection** already compared digit-normalized telephone values; since stored values are now E.164, that comparison is exactly a comparison of E.164 values, so no change was needed there.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 full suite **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
